// Ch1 C1-10 "Kell's stall: the wick" (critical) and the optional side scene "The Sea Owes Me a
// Favour" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch01.md §4). On the way to the dive mooring Rhen passes Mother
// Kell's chandlery on the second mooring, as every diver does. Every path: she presses a fresh wick
// from her own spool into his hand, "For luck", and he pockets it in his tin without looking
// (ch01_has_kell_wick; the chapter flow gives the key item kell_wick). "Stay a minute." is the side
// scene (ch01_kell_side_scene); "Tide's turning, Kell." goes straight on to C1-11.
// O09: 65 mm, her hands and the wick in focus; inserts on her hands in the side scene.
// ADR 0022 watches, every one: her own stock, given as to every diver; not a parting gift, not from
// or about Dace; nothing about Rhen's father; nobody asked her to keep him; the wick is never fitted
// to the lantern. Kell: Low Reaches plain, fond through insults, a trader's arithmetic. No more than
// four of her lines in a row (SPEC §3.6). Her last line in the side scene is her last to him.
title: ch01_kell_stall
location: ch01/oruvel
---
@camera O09
Kell [neutral]: Sallow. Over here. Second dive? #line:ch01_kell_001
Rhen [smile]: Tide's good, and the scale-man's in a robbing mood. I need more brass. #line:ch01_kell_002
@anim kell press_wick
Kell [neutral]: Hand. For luck. #line:ch01_kell_003
@anim rhen pocket_tin
Rhen [neutral]: For luck. #line:ch01_kell_004
<<set $ch01_has_kell_wick = true>>
-> Stay a minute. #line:ch01_kell_005
    <<set $ch01_kell_side_scene = true>>
    <<jump side_scene>>
-> Tide's turning, Kell. #line:ch01_kell_006
    Kell [neutral]: Then go and catch it. #line:ch01_kell_007
@camera release
===
title: side_scene
---
@anim kell trim_wicks
Kell [neutral]: Then make yourself useful. Wicks for the afternoon divers. Even lengths. #line:ch01_kell_008
@anim rhen trim_wicks
Rhen [smile]: Even lengths. I've been doing this since I was eight. #line:ch01_kell_009
@anim kell take_scissors
Kell [neutral]: Badly. Since you were eight, badly. Give those here. #line:ch01_kell_010
Rhen [neutral]: Kell. Why did you never learn to swim? #line:ch01_kell_011
Kell [neutral]: Never needed to. The sea owes me a favour, and I've never once collected. #line:ch01_kell_012
Kell [smile]: It can't take me while it's in debt. Salt and stone, that's plain trade. #line:ch01_kell_013
Rhen [laugh]: That isn't how debt works. #line:ch01_kell_014
Kell [neutral]: It's how mine works. #line:ch01_kell_015
@wait 0.8
Kell [neutral]: Tavi asked you twice to go to Tamsule with the side. Why didn't you? #line:ch01_kell_016
Rhen [smile]: Somebody has to keep you in brass. #line:ch01_kell_017
Kell [neutral]: Hm. #line:ch01_kell_018
@wait 1.0
Kell [smile]: Go on. The tide won't wait for a pretty face, and it won't wait for yours either. #line:ch01_kell_019
@anim rhen laugh
Rhen [laugh]: That's the nicest thing you've said all week. #line:ch01_kell_020
@camera release
===
